{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>I</b> — I have no desire but to behold Your face, for the righteousness I kept was the cause of my delight in seeing Your face. The meaning: to recognize the deeds of HaShem, for they are all comprehensive principles, made with wisdom, and endure forever; and I am sated with the delight of Your form—not as when their belly is filled. And this is not in a dream but in wakefulness, and this vision is not in the sight of the eye but in the sight corresponding to the intellect—for these are true visions of Elohim. And these matters none will understand except one who has studied the wisdom of the soul."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:28.328675290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}